The rules are complete:
- the deal, the bid range 0-3, the simultaneous reveal and the 3 simultaneous tricks are all defined;
- trick resolution is fully specified, including Mermaid+SK+Pirate together, where Mermaid wins and earns +40;
- SK capture bonuses (+20 per Pirate) are defined;
- scoring covers every bid/result combination;
- the game ends after a fixed 8 rounds;
- the winner comes from arithmetic on kept totals.

The declared step count of 12 matches the list exactly: deal, bid, reveal, 3 x (play + resolve), score, announce, end check. There are 4 choice steps (bid + 3 plays), which is within the limit of 4. Attributes 10 ≤ 20, hidden elements 1 ≤ 3, random draws 1 ≤ 1, rounds 8 ≤ 40.

Engine support: the deal uses the shared_deck_draw workaround (supported). Simultaneous polls are used for every joint choice. Trick resolution is calc and conditional operations. No board, clock, judge, trading or binding agreements are needed.

Talk: omitting it is sensible. Bids are a public, costly signal, and every played card is revealed, so players reason from real information rather than guessing. Free talk would add only cheap claims. This is not a cooperation game, so the late-round betrayal check does not apply.
